@participant4 
What do you mean of different domain? Spox should attempt to do version conversion to move the models to a common opset version, you can also try to use `onnx.version_converter` yourself to do that. Is there a specific exception you are getting?

For composing sequentially you can pass the Vars returned by the first in-line call to the next one. For instance `inline(model2)(*inline(model1)(x, y, …).values())` could work, assuming the ordering of outputs of the first model is the same as the ordering of inputs in the second. You can also pass the arguments by name if you need to. I do encourage you to experiment with some simple cases, or share the model signatures you have (input and output types & names).
